====================================================================================
Profile-likelihood uncertainty on theta_w, and what each Fisher estimator claimed
====================================================================================
  set            profile 1-sigma     AD Fisher     FD Fisher   AD error   FD error
  M                  0.02388 deg     0.02389 deg     0.02391 deg       1.0x       1.0x
  M+P+C               0.0218 deg     0.02208 deg     0.02215 deg       1.0x       1.0x

  The 'error' columns are each Fisher estimate divided by the likelihood answer.
  A Cramér–Rao value is a *lower* bound, so a ratio below 1 is mathematically
  legitimate -- but a ratio far below 1 means the bound is loose to the point of
  being misleading if it is read, as it usually is, as the achievable accuracy.
  A ratio above 1 is worse than loose: it is not a valid bound at all, and
  indicates the computed Fisher information is too small.

